  "id": "Compound::DB01435 - Gene::1571",
  "verbalization": "Antipyrine is shown to interact with Cyp2e1 through a series of mechanistic pathways involving Cyp2c19 and Cyp3a4. The evidence suggests that Antipyrine binds to Cyp2c19, which then participates in the arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity, ultimately leading to Cyp2e1 being involved in felbamate metabolism. Similarly, Antipyrine's interaction with Cyp3a4 results in participation in felbamate metabolism, which in turn is linked to Cyp2e1. These pathways collectively indicate that Antipyrine influences Cyp2e1 through the metabolic activation of arachidonic acid and felbamate, both of which are metabolized by Cyp2e1. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, biologically plausible mechanism by which Antipyrine may modulate Cyp2e1 activity. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of cytochrome P450 enzymes in the metabolic processing of Antipyrine's effects, with Cyp2e1 acting as a key enzyme in this process.",
